kamerplanter#1294 — a comment block placed after a trailing `\` truncates the
nuclei command, so `-tags`, `-severity` and both output flags never run. The
step goes red, which looks self-reporting, but `results.jsonl` and
`results.sarif` are never written and the later SARIF upload and issue-opening
steps skip silently behind their own existence guards.

This is the shape nolte/pre-commit-hooks#11 describes as "a clean scan and a
scan that never ran, indistinguishable downstream" (listed there as
kamerplanter#1308, which fixed the downstream half of the same family). It
stands in for kamerplanter#1235, which that issue also named: #1235's defect
lived in scripts/ci/check_digest_freshness.py, outside .github/workflows, and
none of this hook's five shapes has a predicate for it — verified by running
the hook over e0ac3980c^, which reports zero findings in
chart-image-digest-freshness.yml.

  red/    git show 78785f87b^:.github/workflows/security-nuclei-nightly.yml
  green/  git show 78785f87b:.github/workflows/security-nuclei-nightly.yml

  fix     78785f87b  fix(security): stop the nightly Nuclei command from being
                     truncated by a comment (#1294)

Expected: red/ reports `commented_continuation` at line 190 of
security-nuclei-nightly.yml; green/ reports nothing for that file.
